## 1. What {{product.name}} is

{{#example}}**Pocket Garden is a web platform that reminds people to water their plants and shows them what it
noticed.** You add a plant, say how often it drinks, and Pocket Garden tells you when — and, when you
come back, what happened since: which plants were watered, which were skipped, which look overdue.

It is a web platform. People open it in a browser; nothing is downloaded, nothing is installed.
{{/example}}{{^example}}**{{product.name}} is {{product.one_line}}.**

> ✍️ *Two or three sentences: what a person does with it, and what they get back. Write it the way you
> would say it to a customer. This paragraph is quoted by the landing page, the agent's rules and the
> onboarding pages — one text, many renderings.*
{{/example}}
## 2. Who it is for

{{#example}}People who keep a few plants at home and lose track. Not nurseries, not growers, not people with a
greenhouse — someone with six pots on a windowsill who has killed a fern before. English first; one
language until §7 says otherwise.
{{/example}}{{^example}}> ✍️ *Who exactly, and who not. One paragraph. The sharper the "not", the easier every later scope
> decision becomes.*
{{/example}}
